  "implementation": [
    "Only the macOS owned fixture importer uses the public C bridge. Header exposes one OSStatus/count function with no identity/key output; no SPI, symbol injection, dynamic lookup or Swift unavailable declaration bypass.",
    "C checks the actual one passed Keychain, bounded public CFData and maximum16 enumeration, rejects any different leaf or non-unique result, and releases all search/identity/certificate/data Copy/Create references across success/error paths.",
    "Actual producer invokes xcrun --sdk macosx clang -c, then xcrun --sdk macosx swiftc with a formal -import-objc-header and the C object. Either real compiler error remains nonzero; successful C compiler text is added to the existing public compile log, leaving the public output allowlist unchanged.",
    "Swift preserves fresh owned open/unlock/status, strict schema2 reporting, SecItem matching, actual persisted-key challenge sign/verify, certificate fingerprints and codesign-not-yet-proven=false. No global searchlist/trust, account, private key export or certificate-shape change.",
    "Source contracts genuinely grow SDK5to7/fullprobe175to177/finite17to19. All eleven selection method sets, 253definitions/255exact leaves, fixed budgets and existing probe functions remain unchanged."
  ],
